    "purpose": "Read the printer build-date scalar used by the pen subsystem.",
    "control_flow_proof": "A032B2B8 callsA03237B6 and prints its scalar through the standard CLI integer formatter. A0323776 first callsA00089DE. Its gateA0008924 reads20004894; physical60 proves initialized flag1, so it skips initialization. A0008938 performs the previously reviewed software hash/compare on boot RAM. If overrides are permitted, only the fixed scalar DSID0x13FC3 is read usingA03211B4 (bounded current-task cache, otherwise storage getter); there is no transaction unlock or write path. Earlier DS2 returned0 for that override, which is retained as raw evidence because zero alone is ambiguous. When no nonzero override is returned, A03237B6 reads20D02D94. Physical68 proves it is nonzero20180624, so the fallback-provider call and cache write are skipped on the observed state. For completeness the fallback objectA05C5154 has slot12 A02D16AE, a fixedDSID0x13042 scalar read. Earlier direct NVM and DS2 returned the same20180624 for DSID_MFG_DATE_EPOCH. No motors, ink, scanner lighting, setting changes or persistent writes are invoked.",
